	<span><p>By 2025, more than half of all <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com=
/en/software-engineering/insights/how-to-lead-high-performing-software-engi=
neering-teams?utm_medium=3Dpress-release&amp;utm_campaign=3DRM_NA_2023_ITSW=
EL_NPP_PR1_SDTIMESBYLINE">software engineering leader</a>&nbsp;role descrip=
tions will explicitly require oversight of <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.c=
om/en/newsroom/press-releases/2023-08-16-gartner-places-generative-ai-on-th=
e-peak-of-inflated-expectations-on-the-2023-hype-cycle-for-emerging-technol=
ogies">generative artificial intelligence (AI)</a>, according to Gartner, I=
nc.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9COutside of generative AI=E2=80=99s impact on technology impleme=
ntation, it also changes the managerial responsibilities of software engine=
ering leaders,=E2=80=9D said <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/experts/=
haritha-khandabattu">Haritha Khandabattu</a>, Senior Director Analyst at Ga=
rtner. =E2=80=9CThis includes those related to team management, talent mana=
gement and code of ethics. Software engineering leaders will find themselve=
s at a significant disadvantage if they do not recognize and adapt to these=
 changes =E2=80=93 facing the risk of being replaced by those who embrace t=
his disruptive technology.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><strong>Generative AI Requires Software Engineering Leaders to Focus on =
Their Team=E2=80=99s Value<br>
 </strong>When piloting generative AI, software engineering leaders must de=
monstrate the business value of using generative AI to augment their teams.=
 This will help software engineering leaders build a compelling business ca=
se for ongoing investment in their teams.</p>
<p>Software engineering leaders must also be transparent with their teams a=
nd focus conversations on how AI technology will enhance <a href=3D"https:/=
/www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2023-04-24-gartner-survey-finds=
-the-need-to-improve-developer-experience-is-driving-software-engineering-t=
echnology-adoption">developer</a> productivity, rather than focusing on how=
 it will replace staff.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CGenerative AI will not replace developers in the near future,=
=E2=80=9D said Khandabattu. =E2=80=9CWhile it has the ability to automate c=
ertain aspects of software engineering, it cannot replicate the creativity,=
 critical thinking and problem-solving abilities that humans possess. Leade=
rs should reinforce the <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/software-engi=
neering/insights/value-stories-to-communicate-business-value-software-engin=
eering?utm_medium=3Dpress-release&amp;utm_campaign=3DRM_NA_2023_ITSWEL_NPP_=
PR1_SDTIMESBYLINE&amp;utm_term=3Dinfographic">value</a> of their teams by d=
emonstrating how generative AI is a force multiplier that can enhance effic=
iency.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><strong>Generative AI Transforms How Software Engineering Leaders Recrui=
t and Manage Talent<br>
 </strong>Generative AI applications can speed up recruitment and hiring ta=
sks, such as performing a job analysis and transcribing interview summaries=
. For example, software engineering leaders can enter a prompt requesting k=
eywords or key phrases related to skills or experience for platform enginee=
ring.</p>
<p>Software engineering leaders can also invest in generative AI to allocat=
e more time to focus on the people-centric aspects of their role. Investing=
 in generative AI technologies will allow software engineering leaders to c=
ontinuously upskill engineers and cultivate an adaptable workforce.</p>
<p>=E2=80=9CIn addition to recruitment, skill management and development li=
e at the core of leaders=E2=80=99 responsibilities,=E2=80=9D said Khandabat=
tu. =E2=80=9CAI-enabled skills management, a dynamic skills approach that h=
elps in supporting <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/software-engineeri=
ng/insights/how-to-attract-develop-retain-software-engineering-talent?utm_m=
edium=3Dpress-release&amp;utm_campaign=3DRM_NA_2023_ITSWEL_NPP_PR1_SDTIMESB=
YLINE">talent</a> and work processes, will help software engineering leader=
s rethink roles by identifying skills that can be combined to create new po=
sitions and eliminate redundances.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p><strong>Generative AI Introduces Ethical Concerns That Require New Polic=
ies<br>
 </strong>=E2=80=9CThe use of foundational AI models can introduce risks su=
ch as hallucinations, the generation of false yet plausible-seeming content=
, and bias,=E2=80=9D said Khandabattu. =E2=80=9CSoftware engineering leader=
s need to be cautious when using this technology.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>Software engineering leaders must work with, or form, an <a href=3D"http=
s://www.gartner.com/en/articles/ai-ethics">AI ethics</a> committee to creat=
e policy guidelines that help teams responsibly use generative AI tools for=
 design and development. Software engineering leaders play a key role in id=
entifying and helping to mitigate the ethical risks of any generative AI pr=
oducts that are developed in-house or purchased from third-party vendors.</=
p>
<p>=E2=80=9CRefrain from using generative AI to replace tasks that require =
human judgement and critical thinking,=E2=80=9D said Khandabattu. =E2=80=9C=
Constantly evaluate use cases where generative AI can add maximum value in =
day-to-day activities.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>Gartner clients can read more in <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/docu=
ment/4657399">=E2=80=9CGenerative AI Changes Software Engineering Leaders=
=E2=80=99 Responsibilities.=E2=80=9D</a></p>
<p>Learn how to drive higher performance across software engineering teams =
in the complimentary Gartner ebook <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/so=
ftware-engineering/insights/how-to-lead-high-performing-software-engineerin=
g-teams?utm_medium=3Dpress-release&amp;utm_campaign=3DRM_NA_2023_ITSWEL_NPP=
_PR1_SDTIMESBYLINE">How to Lead High Performing Software Engineering Teams.=
</a><br>
</p>
<p><strong>Gartner Application Innovation &amp; Business Solutions Summit<b=
r>
 </strong>Application innovation and software engineering strategies will b=
e discussed at the Gartner Application Innovation &amp; Business Solutions =
Summits taking place September 13-14 in <a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/=
en/conferences/emea/applications-uk">London</a>. Follow news and updates fr=
om the conferences on X using <a href=3D"https://twitter.com/hashtag/Gartne=
rAPPS?src=3Dhashtag_click" target=3D"_blank" title=3D"Twitter">#GartnerAPPS=
</a>.</p>
<p><strong>About Gartner for Software Engineering Leaders</strong><br>
Gartner for Software Engineering Leaders helps leaders align with stakehold=
ers, retain and optimize teams and build innovative products that support a=
nd serve the entire organization, its partners and clients. Additional info=
rmation is available at<a href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/software-engin=
eering"> https://www.gartner.com/en/software-engineering</a>.</p>
<p>Follow news and updates from Gartner for Software Engineering Leaders on=
 <a href=3D"https://twitter.com/Gartner_inc" target=3D"_blank" title=3D"twi=
tter">X</a> and <a href=3D"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/gartner-for-it=
-leaders/" target=3D"_blank" title=3D"linkedin">LinkedIn</a>. Visit the <a =
href=3D"https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/topics/information-technology">=
Gartner Newsroom</a> for more information and insights.<strong> </strong></=
p>
</span>
